Subject: [PATCH 3/5] replicavault: primary-first retainer, primary fallback
 (B1 design i)

The pilot vaulted on the OSD at acting-set rank 1. Two attacker-triggerable
cases left acknowledged deletes unvaulted (phase 2 scenarios a03, a04):
  G1  the acting set has no rank 1 (pool size 1, or min_size 1 with the
      replicas down);
  G2  primary_temp places the primary at acting rank 1, and the primary
      never vaulted.

retainer_osd() replaces acting_rank(): the retainer is element RETAIN_RANK
of the acting set reordered primary-first, or the primary itself when the
acting set has no other member. Replicas (do_repop) and recovery
(remove_missing_object) vault when they are the retainer, as before. New:
the primary vaults in ReplicatedBackend::submit_transaction when it is the
retainer, after issue_op has encoded the replicas' transaction and before
log_operation, as its own txc queued ahead of op_t on the same sequencer,
logged path=fallback. The CRUSH mapping runs only for transactions that
delete a head. No message, peering, PG log, scrub or backfill change.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
